    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0643" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg623"/>

                <head>Lord Lyons to Mr. Seward,.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 2, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the day before yesterday, enclosing a copy of a despatch from
                    Mr. J. Q. Howard, consul of the United States at St. John, New Brunswick,
                    relative to the passage through that city of unusual numbers of persons hostile
                    to the United States en route for Canada. I have, without loss of time, brought
                    the matter to the notice of his excellency the governor general of that
                    province.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
